string automation.opportunityForContactStage(string contactStage)
{
	// =========================================================================
	// _util_opportunityForContactStage   (VERSION: v6-contact-snapshot)
	//
	// The SINGLE authority for "which opportunity type does this Contact Stage
	// represent?" -- the MQL / SQL / FTP / RTP value stamped into the nine Activity
	// context snapshot fields.
	//
	// Per the authoritative commercial model, opportunity authority lives on the
	// CONTACT, not the Deal:
	//     *_Task_Stage        <- the Contact's Stage when the Activity was raised
	//     *_Task_Opportunity  <- the Contact's MQL/SQL/FTP/RTP when it was raised
	//     *_Task_Pipeline     <- the DEAL's relationship Pipeline when it was raised
	//
	// Before this existed the opportunity snapshot was read from Deals.Stage at five
	// sites (processContact, createAuxTask, sendSequencedEmail, handleCallOutcome,
	// handleMeetingEvent), which made a Contact-scoped fact Deal-sourced -- so two
	// Contacts on one Deal recorded the same opportunity type regardless of where
	// each actually was. The map itself is unchanged: it is the vocabulary that was
	// already inlined at routeContactSequence:414-422, lifted to one place and given
	// every caller in the same window.
	//
	// ⚠ Returns "" for a blank or unrecognised Stage. It NEVER defaults. A default
	// here would write a plausible-but-false opportunity type into a permanent
	// historical snapshot, and an out-of-set picklist write is discarded silently
	// anyway. Callers must test for "" and simply omit the key.
	//
	// Deals.Stage remains the Deal's OWN opportunity roll-up and is still written by
	// processDeal. This function does not replace that; it stops Activities from
	// borrowing it.
	// =========================================================================
	s = ifnull(contactStage, "").toString().trim();
	if(s == "") { return ""; }

	m = Map();
	m.put("Marketing Consent", "MQL");
	m.put("Demo Booking", "SQL");
	m.put("Demo Confirmation", "SQL");
	m.put("Demo Hosted", "SQL");
	m.put("Proposal Preparation", "FTP");
	m.put("Commercial Agreement", "FTP");
	m.put("Onboarding", "RTP");
	m.put("Renewal", "RTP");

	return ifnull(m.get(s), "").toString();
}
